      "prompt": "<strong>[Hard] Tukey's IQR Outlier Boundary Filtering</strong><p>Given <code>s = pd.Series([10.0, 12.0, 11.0, 13.0, 12.0, 95.0, 11.0, 10.0, -40.0])</code>: Compute Q1, Q3, and IQR fences. Extract <code>outliers = sorted(s[(s < lo) | (s > hi)].tolist())</code> and count retained values into <code>clean_count = int(s.between(lo, hi).sum())</code>.</p>",
      "ref": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\ns = pd.Series([10.0, 12.0, 11.0, 13.0, 12.0, 95.0, 11.0, 10.0, -40.0])\nq1 = float(s.quantile(0.25))\nq3 = float(s.quantile(0.75))\niqr = q3 - q1\nlo = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\nhi = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\noutliers = sorted(s[(s < lo) | (s > hi)].tolist())\nclean_count = int(s.between(lo, hi).sum())\nprint(f'{outliers=}, {clean_count=}')\n",
