      "desc": "Given Series with a 500.0 spike, calculate IQR fences, winsorize the Series using s.clip(lo, hi) into capped_series, and compute its new mean rounded to 1 decimal place in capped_mean (11.7).",
      "prompt": "<strong>[Hard] Winsorization Outlier Capping via clip()</strong><p>Given <code>s = pd.Series([10.0, 12.0, 11.0, 13.0, 12.0, 11.0, 10.0, 500.0])</code>: Calculate Tukey fences and cap extremes via <code>capped_series = s.clip(lo, hi).round(1).tolist()</code> and <code>capped_mean = float(round(s.clip(lo, hi).mean(), 1))</code>.</p>",
      "ref": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\ns = pd.Series([10.0, 12.0, 11.0, 13.0, 12.0, 11.0, 10.0, 500.0])\nq1 = float(s.quantile(0.25))\nq3 = float(s.quantile(0.75))\niqr = q3 - q1\nlo = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\nhi = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\ncapped_series = s.clip(lo, hi).round(1).tolist()\ncapped_mean = float(round(s.clip(lo, hi).mean(), 1))\nprint(f'{capped_series=}, {capped_mean=}')\n",
      "solution": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\ns = pd.Series([10.0, 12.0, 11.0, 13.0, 12.0, 11.0, 10.0, 500.0])\nq1 = float(s.quantile(0.25))\nq3 = float(s.quantile(0.75))\niqr = q3 - q1\nlo = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\nhi = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\ncapped_series = s.clip(lo, hi).round(1).tolist()\ncapped_mean = float(round(s.clip(lo, hi).mean(), 1))\nprint(f'{capped_series=}, {capped_mean=}')\n",
