      "prompt": "<strong>[Hard] End-to-End Enterprise Cleaning Pipeline</strong><p>Chain operations on <code>raw_data</code>: strip and title-case names, drop duplicates, invalidate age > 100, impute age & salary medians. Extract <code>final_rows = int(len(clean_df))</code>, <code>is_unique_ids = bool(clean_df['id'].is_unique)</code>, and <code>no_nulls = bool(clean_df.isna().sum().sum() == 0)</code>.</p>",
      "ref": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nraw_data = pd.DataFrame({'id': [1, 2, 2, 3, 4], 'name': [' asha ', 'RAVI', 'RAVI', 'Zoya', 'Kabir'], 'age': [29, np.nan, np.nan, 200, 35], 'salary': [52000.0, 61000.0, 61000.0, np.nan, 75000.0]})\nclean_df = (raw_data\n    .assign(name=lambda d: d['name'].str.strip().str.title())\n    .drop_duplicates()\n    .assign(age=lambda d: d['age'].where(d['age'].between(0, 100)))\n    .assign(age=lambda d: d['age'].fillna(d['age'].median()),\n            salary=lambda d: d['salary'].fillna(d['salary'].median()))\n)\nfinal_rows = int(len(clean_df))\nis_unique_ids = bool(clean_df['id'].is_unique)\nno_nulls = bool(clean_df.isna().sum().sum() == 0)\nprint(f'{final_rows=}, {is_unique_ids=}, {no_nulls=}')\n",
      "solution": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nraw_data = pd.DataFrame({'id': [1, 2, 2, 3, 4], 'name': [' asha ', 'RAVI', 'RAVI', 'Zoya', 'Kabir'], 'age': [29, np.nan, np.nan, 200, 35], 'salary': [52000.0, 61000.0, 61000.0, np.nan, 75000.0]})\nclean_df = (raw_data\n    .assign(name=lambda d: d['name'].str.strip().str.title())\n    .drop_duplicates()\n    .assign(age=lambda d: d['age'].where(d['age'].between(0, 100)))\n    .assign(age=lambda d: d['age'].fillna(d['age'].median()),\n            salary=lambda d: d['salary'].fillna(d['salary'].median()))\n)\nfinal_rows = int(len(clean_df))\nis_unique_ids = bool(clean_df['id'].is_unique)\nno_nulls = bool(clean_df.isna().sum().sum() == 0)\nprint(f'{final_rows=}, {is_unique_ids=}, {no_nulls=}')\n",
